      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An account is offered of urgent transfers of patients carried out by the Imperia Hospital's cardiology section in a period of 5 yr. Frequency (1.5% of admitted patients), destination (63% to Genoa, the regional capital), modality (Red Cross ambulance in all but one case), and form of accompaniment (doctor or trained attendant in 81%) are described along with the reasons for the transfer. Of these, 73% were AV block with MAS. It is felt, if the section can be equipped in the future for the installation of permanent pacemakers, the number of such transfers could be cut down to a few cases per year."},
